{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01F2Pdif5n47RySCFvP72nPG", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Brown_(critical_theory)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://english.uchicago.edu/faculty/bill-brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/bill-brown?page=0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/bill-brown?page=1\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/author/B/B/au5561906.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bigthink.com/people/billbrown/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://humanitiesday2014.uchicago.edu/node/356.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://bigthink.com/?p=3384\"}, {\"url\": \"https://alchetron.com/Bill-Brown-(critical-theory)\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:35:10.026Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Bill Brown University of Chicago critical theorist B.A. education", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_011aZxcemEuZE4oP8fGH616d", "content": [{"title": "Bill Brown (critical theory)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Brown_(critical_theory)"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://english.uchicago.edu/faculty/bill-brown"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/bill-brown?page=0"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/bill-brown?page=1"}, {"title": "About the Author", "url": "https://www.press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/author/B/B/au5561906.html"}, {"title": "bigthink.com", "url": "https://bigthink.com/people/billbrown/"}, {"title": "humanitiesday2014.uchicago.edu", "url": "https://humanitiesday2014.uchicago.edu/node/356.html"}, {"title": "bigthink.com", "url": "https://bigthink.com/?p=3384"}, {"title": "Tripti Joshi (Editor)", "url": "https://alchetron.com/Bill-Brown-(critical-theory)"}]}, "The search didn't turn up a B.A. for Bill Brown. The only education details came from Alchetron, a wiki-style site, which lists Duke University as his education. A fragment of the same page says he studied in Stanford University's Modern Thought and Literature program, but it doesn't say whether that was a graduate or undergraduate program, and the snippet is cut off. Neither of these sources names a degree or year.\n\nBackground on his career is better documented. The University of Chicago describes him as the Karla Scherer distinguished service professor in American culture, and his main work is in \"thing theory,\" which borrows from Heidegger's object/thing distinction. He has also co-edited the University of Chicago's peer-reviewed literary journal, Critical Inquiry, since 1993.\n\nFor the B.A. specifically, I'd check the University of Chicago English department faculty page or his CV, which would list his degrees with institutions and years. I didn't run a second search, so that's a suggested next step rather than something I've confirmed."], "durationSeconds": 5.236024958, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01F2Pdif5n47RySCFvP72nPG", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
