{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01Rs5hLp99Uo2m7mBCzeDrAi", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Brown_(critical_theory)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thing_theory\"}, {\"url\": \"https://english.uchicago.edu/faculty/bill-brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://english.uchicago.edu/bill-brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://modernismmodernity.org/tags/thing-theory\"}, {\"url\": \"https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/bill-brown?page=0\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.amacad.org/person/bill-brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://develop-plus.bigthink.com/?p=3384\"}, {\"url\": \"https://develop.bigthink.com/?p=3384\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:35:19.301Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"Bill Brown\" \"thing theory\" B.A. Duke University Ph.D. Stanford Modern Thought and Literature", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_015rT4E8YrrzPuxZ7J2bjPru", "content": [{"title": "Bill Brown (critical theory)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Brown_(critical_theory)"}, {"title": "Thing theory", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thing_theory"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://english.uchicago.edu/faculty/bill-brown"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://english.uchicago.edu/bill-brown"}, {"title": "thing theory", "url": "https://modernismmodernity.org/tags/thing-theory"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://news.uchicago.edu/profile/bill-brown?page=0"}, {"title": "bill brown", "url": "https://www.amacad.org/person/bill-brown"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://develop-plus.bigthink.com/?p=3384"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://develop.bigthink.com/?p=3384"}]}, "The search supports the Stanford link and the thing theory work, but not the Duke B.A.\n\n- **Stanford:** A Wikipedia snippet on Bill Brown (critical theory) mentions Stanford University's Modern Thought and Literature program. The snippet is cut off, so it doesn't say whether this was his doctorate. I found nothing about Duke.\n- **Teaching:** The same page says he has taught at the University of Chicago since 1989 (He has been teaching at the University of Chicago since 1989.).\n- **Thing theory:** The Wikipedia article on thing theory credits him with largely creating the field. It contrasts objects, which have a clear known use, with things, which show themselves when they break down or resist our understanding (For University of Chicago Professor Bill Brown, objects are items for which subjects have a known and clear sense of place, use and role. Things, on the other hand, manifest themselves once they interact with our bodies unexpectedly, break down, malfunction, shed their encoded social values, or elude our understanding.). The same article notes he edited a 2001 Critical Inquiry special issue and wrote *A Sense of Things* (The theory was largely created by Prof. Brown, who edited a special issue of Critical Inquiry on it in 2001 and published a monograph on the subject entitled A Sense of Things.).\n- **Recognition:** The American Academy of Arts and Sciences profile says his work has achieved internationally-recognized authority in the field of thing theory. It also lists his election in 2018.\n\nGap: nothing I retrieved confirms a Duke B.A. or the year and title of a Stanford Ph.D. A check of his CV or a university bio would settle that."], "durationSeconds": 6.362417958, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01Rs5hLp99Uo2m7mBCzeDrAi", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
