{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01PsQwLHc9YDV99fxEtVxF8x", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Brown_(critical_theory)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._Marvin_Brown\"}, {\"url\": \"http://chronicle.uchicago.edu/040923/dsp-named-faculty.shtml\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judy_Brown_(professor)\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerry_B._Brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendy_Brown\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thing_theory\"}, {\"url\": \"https://hq.humanities.uci.edu/complit/culturesofviolence/keynotes.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://english.uchicago.edu/bill-brown\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:35:36.060Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"Bill Brown\" critical theory Wikipedia \"received his B.A.\"", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01MSKmgoH2mNy4CbGUdK8Nak", "content": [{"title": "Bill Brown (critical theory)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Brown_(critical_theory)"}, {"title": "J. Marvin Brown", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/J._Marvin_Brown"}, {"title": "Faculty members named to new professorships", "url": "http://chronicle.uchicago.edu/040923/dsp-named-faculty.shtml"}, {"title": "Judy Brown (professor)", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judy_Brown_(professor)"}, {"title": "Jerry B. Brown", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerry_B._Brown"}, {"title": "Wendy Brown", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendy_Brown"}, {"title": "Thing theory", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thing_theory"}, {"title": "hq.humanities.uci.edu", "url": "https://hq.humanities.uci.edu/complit/culturesofviolence/keynotes.html"}, {"title": "Bill Brown", "url": "https://english.uchicago.edu/bill-brown"}]}, "The search didn't return the \"received his B.A.\" sentence from the Wikipedia article itself. The Wikipedia snippet covers Brown's current role as Karla Scherer distinguished service professor at the University of Chicago and his work on American literature and modernism. It also says he has co-edited *Critical Inquiry* since 1993.\n\nThe education details come from a University of Chicago Chronicle piece (around 2004, so possibly dated). It reports that Brown earned his bachelor's degree at Duke University, and that he later got an M.A. in creative writing and a Ph.D. in modern thought and literature, both from Stanford.\n\nThe Wikipedia article on \"Thing theory\" also links Brown to the field. It credits him with largely developing the theory, editing a 2001 special issue of *Critical Inquiry* on it, and writing the monograph *A Sense of Things*."], "durationSeconds": 5.098913540999998, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01PsQwLHc9YDV99fxEtVxF8x", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
